  "notes": "Verified 2026-09-17 by fetching the real archived 2022-23 bulletin page directly (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2022-2023/.../communication-sciences-disorders-bs/). The Program Requirements course list (all 29 codes across the CSD prescribed courses, PSYCH 100, and the EDPSY 14/PSYCH 261, HDFS 129/PSYCH 212, STAT 200/EDPSY 101/PSYCH 200, and HDFS 229/249N/315/411/418/432/PSYCH 270/471 pools) is byte-identical to CSD-2026.json's -- the actual CSD-specific course requirements have not changed since 2022. What genuinely differs is the Gen Ed *scaffolding* around those courses: 2022-23 is the last catalog year before Penn State's Gen Ed reform introduced the 'Integrative Studies: Inter-Domain' and 'Exploration' categories (first appearing, unlabeled, in the 2023-24 edition -- see CSD-2023.json's notes -- and fully labeled from 2024-25 on). The archived 2022-23 Suggested Academic Plan uses the old Gen Ed category set instead (GA appears twice, GH twice, GHW twice, GQ twice, and GN three times: once each for Human Biological, Physical Science, and a third unrestricted GN slot), and those slots land in different semesters than the 2023-26 files' Inter-Domain/Exploration/GA slots -- most notably, GN Physical Science sits in Semester 5 (Year 3 Fall) here rather than Semester 3, and there is a real extra 3-credit Elective in that same semester the later editions do not have (the page's own printed subtotal for that semester is 16.5-18, versus 15 in every later year). Semester 1 also lists First-Year Seminar as two separate 1-credit courses (CSD 297 and PSU 14, both real, cataloged courses -- same transitional pattern as 2023-24, see CSD-2023.json's notes), and Semester 6's GWS line explicitly lists ENGL 202C and 202D as additional real, cataloged options alongside 202A/202B (dropped from the Suggested Plan's text starting the following year, though the underlying GWS Gen Ed requirement itself is unaffected). Semester 2's archived text lists a bare 'CAS 100' option in addition to 100A/100B/100C; this app's catalog (Backend/catalogs/cas_catalog.json) has no plain 'CAS 100' entry (only 100A/100B/100C/100S), and it is fully redundant with the three options already listed, so it was not added as an uncataloged fallback. Semester 8 keeps CSD-2026.json's existing 3-item simplification (see that item's own comment above) rather than the archived page's literal 5-item table, since that simplification is a pre-existing app convention, not a real 2022-specific requirement change. The page's own printed total credit range is 121-126 (versus 120-124 for 2024-26 and exactly 120 for 2023), consistent with the one extra elective found in Semester 5.",
